Spec: Integration Design Specification

Purpose:
  Own the focused design documents that define the Spec Kit and SpecDD responsibility split, bridge architecture, lifecycle semantics, and v0.1 acceptance contract.

Structure:
  ./spec.md: Design overview, goals, conceptual model, authority classes, and summary invariant
  ./spec-architecture.md: Change Boundary, task, adapter, and deterministic-versus-agentic architecture
  ./spec-lifecycle.md: Lifecycle commands, evolution, convergence, promotion, and governance separation
  ./spec-v0.1.md: v0.1 scope, fixture scenarios, acceptance criteria, design principles, and future direction

Owns:
  ./spec.md
  ./spec-architecture.md
  ./spec-lifecycle.md
  ./spec-v0.1.md

References:
  ../speckit-specdd.sdd
  ./change-boundary.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/extension.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/workflow-overlay.sdd
  ../integration/specdd-preset/specdd-preset.sdd

Must:
  Spec Kit remains authoritative for feature and implementation intent.
  SpecDD remains authoritative for persistent system intent, ownership, modification authority, dependencies, and durable local contracts.
  The Spec Kit constitution remains authoritative for development governance.
  Derived bridge state remains reconstructible and does not become a second persistent copy of SpecDD constraints.
  Specification and authority evolution remain explicit lifecycle transitions rather than retroactive permission for an existing implementation operation.
  The focused documents avoid duplicating detailed command procedures already owned by command and lifecycle guides.

Done when:
  A maintainer can navigate from the overview to one focused document for architecture, lifecycle semantics, or v0.1 acceptance without reading one oversized project specification.
